  "definition": "Aged 16 to 24 with no employment or self-employment income in the year and not recorded as in full-time education, under current law.",
  "definition_notes": [
    "A static estimate: the UC health element and PIP are removed with no replacement benefit modelled and no one moving into work.",
    "The survey data has no NEET flag, so the group is approximated from earnings and the data's full-time education input.",
    "The education input is true for everyone the data records as enrolled at any stage, so part-time students count as in education.",
    "Earnings are for the whole year: someone out of work now who worked earlier in the year is not counted. A small number of people the data records as in approved training, or as working some hours with no earnings, are counted.",
    "The ONS figure is a point-in-time Labour Force Survey estimate (April to June 2026) on its own definition; ours is a modelled population for the fiscal year shown. The two are not like for like.",
    "Each person takes their household's change in net income, as in the dashboard's results by age. A household loses when its net income falls by more than 0.01% of its baseline.",
    "A person personally loses a benefit when their own PIP falls, or they are the claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity in a benefit unit on Universal Credit whose health element falls. Each person is counted once.",
    "Figures resting on fewer than 100 survey records are withheld."
  ],
